    <bpmn:process id="W_W4352" name="W4352. Customer Returns, Plant Guarantee &amp; Replacement Policy" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer return/claim (dead/declined plant under guarantee)
Frequency: Per return/claim
Volume: Live-goods returns/claims (proportional to guarantee take-up)
Owner: Customer Service (VS-13) / Garden Ops / Returns (VS-32)
Participants: Customer Service (VS-13), Garden Ops, Returns (VS-32), Store Ops (VS-07), Finance (VS-118)
Source: workflow W4352 — Customer Returns, Plant Guarantee &amp; Replacement Policy</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4352_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4352_Lane1" name="Garden Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4352_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4352_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4352_Lane2" name="Customer Service">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4352_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4352_Lane3" name="Returns">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4352_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4352_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4352_Start5" name="Customer return/claim (dead/declined plant under guarantee)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4352_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4352_Task6" name="Garden Buyer/Finance set the plant guarantee policy (guarantee period…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Garden Buyer/Finance set the plant guarantee policy (guarantee period, replacement-vs-refund, customer-care-burden, exclusions) balancing service vs abuse
Responsible (R): Garden Buyer / Finance
Accountable (A): Head of Merch / CFO
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4352_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4352_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4352_Task7" name="Customer Service/Garden Ops process the return/claim — verify…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer Service/Garden Ops process the return/claim — verify eligibility/receipt, assess cause (stock-quality vs customer-care), and replace/refund per policy
Responsible (R): Customer Service / Garden Ops
Accountable (A): Store Mgr / Garden Ops Lead
Duration: Per claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4352_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4352_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4352_Task8" name="Returns/Finance route the returned plant to disposal/compost (W4355) or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Returns/Finance route the returned plant to disposal/compost (W4355) or vendor-claim (W4338), track guarantee cost/abuse, and feed prevention
Responsible (R): Returns / Finance
Accountable (A): Returns Lead / CFO
Duration: Per claim</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4352_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4352_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4352_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4352_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-666 (ensure controlled execution — In-Store Garden Center Care, Merchandising &amp; Sell-Through (PA-145.2).) | - CTL-666: guarantee policy applied; cause assessed; abuse monitored; returned plant routed per disposition
Owner: Customer Service (VS-13) / Garden Ops / Returns (VS-32)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
